<title>USA: Delaware transport agency seeks $130 mln more aid.</title>
<headline>Delaware transport agency seeks $130 mln more aid.</headline>
<dateline>DOVER 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Delaware Department of Transportation has asked the state for an additional $130 million over six years.</p>
<p>Del-DOT Secretary Ann Canby told lawmakers on the Joint Bond Bill Committee Thursday that more funds are needed if the state's roads are to remain in good condition.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
